  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2} & <-{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}+x\\cdot {7}^{4x+2} & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{4x+1}+7x\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+7x)\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0 \\\\ x(x+7)\\cdot {7}^{4x+1} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${7}^{4x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x+7)<0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-7$ and $x=0.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-7<x<0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013930/assets/b884ee15f864bcd02639085dc1465a82958ef0faeb9408e68b405c5906ea3a18.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-7<x<0.$",
